From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:18:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma: drop the timer's
 clock-frequency

zuma's firmware programs CNTFRQ_EL0: it reads 24576000 on a Pixel 8
Pro booted with this tree, the same 24.576 MHz the property gave. The
arch timer binding asks for clock-frequency only where firmware leaves
CNTFRQ unset, so drop it, as gs101 does.

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro: without the property the arch timer still runs
at 24.57 MHz, CNTFRQ_EL0 reads 24576000, and the uptime kept pace with
the host's clock over 30 s.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
index 34f702756..046ffbd28 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
@@ -150,8 +150,6 @@ timer {
 			     <GIC_PPI 14 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>,
 			     <GIC_PPI 11 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>,
 			     <GIC_PPI 10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
-		/* Stock sets it: 24.576 MHz. */
-		clock-frequency = <24576000>;
 	};
 
 	/*
